  chrome-agent's core (instance registry, liveness model, launcher,
  supervisor, session, attach, CDP client/protocol, fingerprint, and the
  domains/ typed CDP bindings) is copied into src/browser_tools/core/ per
  RFC-01 (docs/rfc/01_merge-chrome-agent-core-into-browser-tools.rfc.md),
  "Vendoring rules". Each vendored file carries its own attribution header.
  The vendored core is a hard fork: browser-tools does not depend on
  chrome-agent at runtime and may cherry-pick upstream fixes at its
  discretion. chrome-agent's cli.py and __main__.py are not vendored.

